    {
      "id": "s5",
      "title": "Two pattern languages",
      "text": "The trap: globs and regexes are different languages. In a regex, *any characters* is `.*`, and a lone `*` means *repeat the thing before me*. So `grep -E \"*.csv\"` is an error (plain grep quietly finds nothing).",
      "emphasize": [
        "warn",
        "term",
        "parts"
      ],
      "dim": [
        "tree"
      ],
      "set": {
        "term": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "kind": "cmd",
              "text": "grep -E \"*.csv\" inbox.txt"
            },
            {
              "kind": "err",
              "text": "grep: repetition-operator operand invalid",
              "mark": true
            },
            {
              "kind": "cmd",
              "text": "grep -E \".*csv\" inbox.txt"
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Attached: sales.csv and orders.csv.",
              "mark": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "parts": {
          "title": "Any characters, in a regex",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": ".",
              "label": "any one character",
              "tone": "wild"
            },
            {
              "text": "*",
              "label": "repeated, any number of times",
              "tone": "how"
            }
          ],
          "gloss": "So a regex says *any characters* as `.*`. A glob says it as `*`."
        },
        "warn": {
          "tone": "warn",
          "title": "Two pattern languages",
          "md": "In a file name (a glob), `*` means *any characters*. In a regex that's `.*`; a lone `*` means *repeat the thing before me*."
        },
        "page": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "From: dana.lee@example.com"
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Invoice INV-20417 paid on 2026-03-14."
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Please resend INV-20418; the PDF was blank."
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Globex says INV-2042 is still open."
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Attached: sales.csv and orders.csv",
                  "mark": "hit"
                },
                {
                  "t": "."
                }
              ],
              "state": "lit"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Next payment run: 2026/03/20."
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            },
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Note: INV-99999 is only a test number."
                }
              ],
              "state": "dim"
            }
          ],
          "note": "1 line"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "title": "sed swaps text",
      "text": "`sed` swaps text as it passes through. `s/Acme Corp/Acme/g` reads: find *Acme Corp*, put *Acme* in its place, every time. It prints a changed copy; the file stays as it was.",
      "emphasize": [
        "term",
        "parts"
      ],
      "dim": [
        "tree",
        "warn"
      ],
      "set": {
        "term": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "kind": "cmd",
              "text": "cat notes.txt"
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Acme Corp renewal is due in May."
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Send Acme Corp the Q3 report."
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Globex wants a call on Friday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "cmd",
              "text": "sed 's/Acme Corp/Acme/g' notes.txt"
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Acme renewal is due in May.",
              "mark": true
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Send Acme the Q3 report.",
              "mark": true
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "Globex wants a call on Friday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "note",
              "text": "(notes.txt itself is unchanged: sed printed a changed copy)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "parts": {
          "title": "Reading a sed swap",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "s",
              "label": "swap",
              "tone": "how"
            },
            {
              "text": "/"
            },
            {
              "text": "Acme Corp",
              "label": "find this",
              "tone": "exact"
            },
            {
              "text": "/"
            },
            {
              "text": "Acme",
              "label": "put this instead",
              "tone": "wild"
            },
            {
              "text": "/"
            },
            {
              "text": "g",
              "label": "every time on the line",
              "tone": "how"
            }
          ],
          "gloss": "Find *Acme Corp*, put *Acme* in its place: `Acme Corp called` → `Acme called`."
        },
        "page": {
          "title": "notes.txt",
          "lines": [
            {
              "parts": [
                {
                  "t": "Acme Corp",
                  "mark": "hit"
                },
