    {
      "id": "s8",
      "title": "Claude uses both",
      "text": "On a Mac, Claude Code finds files by name with a glob (`find . -name \"*.csv\"`; the quotes let find do the matching) and searches inside them with regexes. You don't need to write these: knowing them lets you ask for them, and spot them when Claude runs them.",
      "show": "*",
      "set": {
        "term": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "kind": "cmd",
              "text": "find . -name \"*.csv\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "./orders.csv"
            },
            {
              "kind": "out",
              "text": "./sales.csv"
            }
          ],
          "badge": "run by Claude"
        },
        "tree": {
